From 860c7a9657f8ae7b55653375916a4768a3aad32f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raing5Days <M202574102@hust.edu.cn>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:55:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v1): close the runtime-key capture lifecycle (bounded,
 synchronized, fail-closed)

Address PR #264 review blockers:

- _dispatch_runtime_key now follows a bounded, synchronized capture
  lifecycle: an already-admitted key replays safely, a brand-new key is
  admitted only while the startup capture window is open, and once
  capturing is disabled dispatch fails closed to eager with the runtime
  metadata preserved on the no-graph descriptor. Registering a key can
  no longer be mistaken for owning a replayable graph.
- Wire Platform.get_cudagraph_key_strategy() into admission: None keeps
  neutral core behavior; a rejecting/failing/protocol-violating strategy
  fails closed. Offset/variant construction, capture scheduling and
  eviction stay owned by the platform plugin.
- Bound runtime keys per mode (MAX_RUNTIME_GRAPH_KEYS_PER_MODE) and make
  admission atomic under a lock for concurrent replay workers.
- Host tests: no-plugin equivalence, strategy missing/rejection/failure
  fallback, duplicate-key idempotency, pre-registered replay after the
  capture window, post-startup fail-closed, key-count bound and
  concurrent registration safety. Wrapper-level integration regression
  proves capture-before-replay and post-startup fail-closed (CUDA gated).
- full_graph_parallel_test.py: no hardcoded model, env/CLI overrides,
  failed requests fail loudly with non-zero exit, optional JSONL
  transcript for paired baseline-vs-plugin diffing.
